  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "### Added\n\n- C# bindings for OCCT 8.0.1, generated by netocc-generator, one namespace per OCCT package (`OCC.Core.<Package>`), OCCT names unchanged: all 362 packages of the FoundationClasses, ModelingData, ModelingAlgorithms, ApplicationFramework and DataExchange modules and of Visualization's TKService, TKV3d, TKOpenGl and TKMeshVS:\n  - geometry, topology and modeling algorithms (booleans, fillets, offsets, sweeps, shape healing, meshing, HLR);\n  - OCAF and XCAF documents;\n  - STEP, IGES, STL, glTF, OBJ, PLY and VRML;\n  - visualization: `AIS`, `V3d`, `Graphic3d`, `Prs3d`, `StdPrs`, `SelectMgr`, `MeshVS`, `Font`, `Image` and the OpenGL driver. `Aspect_Window.FromNativeHandle(handle, display)` wraps a native window (an HWND, an X11 window, an NSView) for `V3d_View.SetWindow`.\n\n  Members that don't map to C# yet are left out.\n- Handles map to proxy objects (`Handle(T)` ⇄ `T`, `T.DownCast`). A `Handle(T)&` is a `ref T` that keeps its proxy unless OCCT puts another object there, also when the call throws or an argument fails its check.\n- NCollection arrays, lists and sequences are C# classes named by OCCT's aliases (`TColgp_Array1OfPnt`, `TopTools_ListOfShape`, `TColStd_HArray1OfReal`), including `TColgp`, `TColGeom` and `TColGeom2d`, which OCCT 8 dropped as packages:\n  - indexers with OCCT's bounds (sequences from 1), `IEnumerable<T>` and `Count`;\n  - arrays of numbers and value types copy to and from C# arrays in one step (`new TColgp_Array1OfPnt(points)`, `ToArray()`);\n  - the handle-managed variants (`TColgp_HArray1OfPnt`) are subclasses of their collection that pass as handles;\n  - maps too (`TopTools_IndexedMapOfShape`, `TopTools_DataMapOfShapeListOfShape`), with indexers by key or number and `KeyValuePair` enumeration.\n- `math_Vector` and `math_IntegerVector` with indexers, bulk copies and arithmetic operators.\n- OCCT 8's vectors (`NCollection_LinearVector`, `NCollection_DynamicArray`) and open-addressing maps (`NCollection_FlatMap`, `NCollection_FlatDataMap`) as collections; a collection OCCT names no alias for is named after its arguments (`NCollection_Array1_BRepGraph_NodeId`, `OCC.Core.NCollection.NCollection_DynamicArray_int`).\n- Other class template instances are classes too, named by an OCCT alias (`IntPolyh_ArrayOfPoints`) or after their arguments (`BRepGraph_MutGuard_BRepGraphInc_VertexDef`). Move-only ones return by value (`using var guard = editor.Mut(vertex)`).\n- OCCT 8's range-for iterators are `IEnumerable<T>`: `foreach (var face in new TopExp_Explorer(shape, TopAbs_FACE))`.\n- Value types are C# structs with OCCT's memory layout: all of `gp` (points, vectors, axes, transformations, lines, circles, planes, quadrics, ...), `Bnd_Box`, `Bnd_Box2d`, `Quantity_Color`, `Quantity_ColorRGBA` and `Poly_Triangle`. Their methods run OCCT's code (trivial math is managed), and OCCT's `+ - * / ^` are C# operators; `gp` itself is a static class (`gp.Origin()`).\n- Nested and namespace types have flat names (`Geom_Curve::ResD1` is `Geom_Curve_ResD1`, `gp_Dir::D` is `gp_Dir_D`). Plain data, such as OCCT 8's evaluation results, is a C# struct with public fields (`curve.EvalD1(u).Point`); enums keep their C++ underlying type.\n- OCCT 8's `BRepGraph`: typed ids are structs (`BRepGraph_FaceId`, `id.Index`), and the node iterators are classes (`new BRepGraph_FaceIterator(graph)`).\n- C++ references are `ref` parameters, enum references included.\n- Raw pointers: a class pointer is its proxy (`null` for `nullptr`; a returned one borrows from its owner, a transient's owns a reference), `T*&` a `ref` of the proxy. Pointers to numbers and structs are C# arrays pinned for the call (`MathUtils.SortRoots(roots, n)`, `obb.GetVertex(corners)`); `void*`, function pointers and pointers a constructor or setter keeps are `IntPtr`. `Standard_ExtString` is a UTF-16 `string`, `const char*&` a `ref string`, and a `Standard_OStream*` a lent stream.\n- What an object keeps a reference to stays alive with it, so no `GC.KeepAlive` is needed:\n  - constructor arguments: `new BRepGraph_FaceIterator(graph)`, a boolean's shared `BOPAlgo_PaveFiller`, adaptor tools and their curves, VRML nodes and their scene;\n  - member arguments: `extrema.Initialize(surface, ...)`, until the next call replaces them;\n  - the object a returned guard or iterator points into: `editor.Mut(vertex)` keeps the graph;\n  - the object a returned view refers to: `graph.Topo()` keeps the graph, `viewer.ActiveViewIterator()` the viewer.\n\n  What a constructor keeps, and the object behind a returned guard, outlive the finalizer too: a guard dropped without `Dispose` is safe.\n- All of BRepMesh, with its triangulation data structures (`BRepMesh_Triangle`, `BRepMesh_DataStructureOfDelaun`): a C array by reference (`int (&)[3]`) is a C# array of that length.\n- `ShapeProcess.ToOperationFlag(name, ref known)` maps an operation name to its flag.\n- `char32_t` is a `uint` (a UTF-32 code point), and a member's `size_t&` return a `ref UIntPtr`. A `size_t` is a `ulong`: on x86 a value above 32 bits throws `OcctException` (`Standard_OutOfRange`), as for C `long`.\n- `char` is its `byte`, by value too (`TCollection_HAsciiString.Value(1)`): its bits, not a character through a code page.\n- References of every fixed-width integer, `char` (its byte), `size_t`, C `long` (a C# `long`, range-checked where `long` is 32-bit) and `Standard_GUID` (`ref Guid`) are `ref` parameters, and a transient passed by `T&` is its proxy; byte-sized ref returns write through (`color.x() = 200`).\n- A C++ call only one overload takes is wrapped even where other arities are ambiguous (`new IntPolyh_ArrayOfPoints()`), and a transient OCCT returns by value comes back as a proxy that owns it (`BRepGraph_Tool_Edge.CurveAdaptor(graph, edge)`).\n- Standard library types: `std::string`, `std::string_view` and string streams are strings; `std::array` is a C# array (`box.Center()`), `std::optional` a nullable (`range.Min()`), `std::bitset` a `ulong` mask (shape-processing flags), `std::pair` a class with `First` and `Second`, `std::complex<double>` an `OCC.Core.Complex`.\n- Strings: `TCollection_AsciiString` is UTF-8 and `TCollection_ExtendedString` UTF-16; `Standard_GUID` maps to `System.Guid`.\n- C++ streams are `System.IO.Stream` parameters (`BRepTools.Write(shape, stream)`, `DumpJson`), lent for the call; readers leave a seekable stream where they stopped.\n- Classes without declared constructors can be created (`new BRep_Builder()`).\n- References a member returns write through: numbers, enums and structs as C# `ref` returns (`fix.FixReorderMode() = 1`), classes and collections as proxies that borrow the object and keep its owner alive (`block.ChangeShapes().Append(shape)`). Members that return their own object for chaining return `void`.\n- What OCCT deprecates is wrapped and `[Obsolete]`, so C# callers get the compiler warning C++ callers get (`Geom_BSplineCurve.Poles(array)`, `Message_ProgressSentry`).\n- Overloads C# can't tell apart reach the most capable one: `ref` returns (`matrix.Value(1, 2) = 5.0`) and UTF-16 strings (`new TCollection_HExtendedString(text)` keeps non-ASCII text). OCCT's `GetType()` (curve and surface types) hides `object.GetType()`.\n- IntelliSense shows OCCT's documentation: the package's XML documentation holds the doc comments of OCCT's headers for the members they document (summaries, parameters, return values, notes, code), next to NetOcc's own. That text is OCCT's, so the package's license is `MIT AND LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0`.\n- A documentation site with a guide, every example compiled and run against the package: [paulbuechner.github.io/netocc](https://paulbuechner.github.io/netocc/), the packages' project URL.\n- A README on nuget.org: requirements, an example, links to the documentation.\n- Versions name the OCCT version the bindings are generated for, with NetOcc's revision: `8.0.1.1` is the first release for OCCT 8.0.1.\n- OCCT exceptions surface as `OcctException`; `e.Is<Standard_DomainError>()` tells whether OCCT raised that class or a subclass. The exception classes themselves are classes (`Standard_OutOfRange`).\n- OCAF documents stay valid while any label, attribute or `TNaming_Builder` proxy lives.\n- One AnyCPU assembly for .NET Framework 3.5 to 4.8, .NET 6, 8 and 10, and netstandard2.0.\n- Natives for win-x64, win-x86, linux-x64 and osx-arm64, one package each (`NetOcc.runtime.<rid>`).",
